      "content": "That's a really useful clue. Caffeine withdrawal headaches tend to start a day or so after cutting back and can hang around for several days. They're usually dull and on both sides, like you're describing. Taper rather than stopping cold, keep hydrated, and an over-the-counter painkiller is reasonable if it's safe for you.",
